@startuml CryptoWeb-E3-layered-conditionalorders
title CryptoWeb - Conditional Orders and Scheduled Execution (LAYERED view)

!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 75
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
hide circle


package "Server_3 HTTP layer" {
  class "Order Routes" as OR <<router>> {
    +post()
    +get()
    +put()
    +delete()
  }
  class "Order Controller" as OC <<controller module>> {
    +postorder()
    +getorders()
    +updateorder()
    +deleteorder()
  }
}

package "Execution and integration" {
  class "Order Executor" as OE <<scheduled job module>> {
    +shouldExecute()
    +markPending()
    +markExecuted()
    +markFailed()
  }
  class "Live Price Service" as LP <<service module>> {
    +getPrice()
  }
  class "Core Gateway" as GW <<HTTP gateway module>> {
    +executeInternalTrade()
  }
  class "Core Trade Controller" as CT <<controller module>> {
    +executeInternal()
  }
  class "Core Trade Service" as TS <<service module>> {
    +buy()
    +sell()
  }
}

package "MongoDB domain models" {
  class "Order" as O <<Mongoose model>> {
    +userId
    +orderType
    +side
    +qty
    +price
    +status
    +ocoGroupId
  }
  class "Trade" as T <<Mongoose model>> {
    +referenceId
    +orderId
    +fillId
    +price
  }
}

OR ..> OC : routes
OC ..> O : create/update
OE ..> O : claim/update
OE ..> LP : get trigger price
OE ..> GW : execute when triggered
GW ..> CT : Core internal REST
CT ..> TS : settle
OE ..> T : upsert fill projection
T "0..*" --> "0..1" O : optional orderId

legend bottom
Order.price is the user-specified trigger price. Trade.price is the market execution price.
The optional MongoDB orderId reference is not unique-enforced.
endlegend

@enduml
